  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is projected at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> to the horizontal as given in the figure. The magnitude of the angular momentum of the particle about the starting point at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is ______.</p><p>(Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9242892d-1de7-42ac-888e-b6d32f29a7bb-9895103.PNG\" style=\"width: 241px; height: 185px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "800",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As torque due to gravitational force will be variable, therefore we can use</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>&#964;</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math>.</p><p>Now, torque of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;at time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;and horizontal velocity of the projectile will remain constant<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>cos</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>800</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn></math>.</p>",
